<title>AUSTRALIA: Cudgen to pay dividend, seek wind-up.</title>
<headline>Cudgen to pay dividend, seek wind-up.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cudgen Resources RZ Ltd said on Tuesday it expected to declare a final dividend in its statement for 1996/97 to June 30 and would ask shareholders to consider a voluntary winding up of the company.</p>
<p>Cudgen, 76.7 percent owned by fellow miner RGC Ltd following a 1996 takeover, said its only remaining asset of significance was a 50 percent stake in Consolidated Rutile Ltd. &quot;The board believes that in this circumstance, it is inappropriate to maintain the company and a stock exchange listing,&quot; Cudgen said.</p>
</text>
